 1044 2469.23 166 268.18Laporan Status Pasaran Harta | 10\nL262@P9: PROPERTY MARKET STATUS REPORT 2024\nL263@P9: 1.0 HARTA TANAH KEDIAMAN\nL264@P9: 1.1 Pelancaran Baru Skim Perumahan\nL265@P9: Pelancaran baharu kediaman pada separuh\nL266@P9: pertama 2026 agak perlahan berbanding\nL267@P9: tempoh yang sama tahun sebelumnya di mana\nL268@P9: berkurangan 25.3% kepada 27,832 unit (H1\nL269@P9: 2025: 37,250 unit). Prestasi jualan dicatatkan\nL270@P9: pada paras 16.6%.\nL271@P9: Kediaman bertanah membentuk 55.6% (15,480\nL272@P9: unit) daripada jumlah pelancaran baharu,\nL273@P9: manakala kediaman strata merekodkan 44.4%\nL274@P9: (12,352 unit).\nL275@P9: Trend pelancaran baharu kediaman bagi H1\nL276@P9: 2023 hingga H1 2026 seperti Carta 1.\nL277@P9: Pada separuh pertama 2026, bilangan\nL278@P9: pelancaran baharu paling tinggi dicatatkan di\nL279@P9: Selangor iaitu sebanyak 8,354 unit, diikuti Johor\nL280@P9: dan Pulau Pinang masing-masing sebanyak\nL281@P9: 6,697 unit dan 2,878 unit.\nL282@P9: Jenis kediaman kondominium/pangsapuri\nL283@P9: mendominasi bilangan pelancaran baharu\nL284@P9: bagi separuh pertama 2026 sebanyak 41.4%.\nL285@P9: Manakala jenis rumah teres dua hingga tiga\nL286@P9: tingkat dan rumah teres satu tingkat masing\u0002masing sebanyak 31.7% dan 15.2%.\nL287@P9: Harta tanah kediaman berharga RM500,001\nL288@P9: hingga RM1,000,000 mendominasi pasaran\nL289@P9: pelancaran baharu pada kadar 57.1% (15,905\nL290@P9: unit), diikuti 28.2% bagi harta tanah berharga\nL291@P9: RM300,000 dan ke bawah (7,856 unit), 12.7%\nL292@P9: untuk harta tanah berharga RM300,001 hingga\nL293@P9: RM500,000 (3,534 unit) dan selebihnya\nL294@P9: merangkumi harta tanah berharga melebihi\nL295@P9: RM1,000,000 (537 unit).\nL296@P9: 1.0 RESIDENTIAL PROPERTY\nL297@P9: 1.1 Newly Launched Housing Scheme\nL298@P9: Newly launched housing scheme in the first\nL299@P9: half of 2026 has been relatively slow compared\nL300@P9: to the same period last year, experiencing a\nL301@P9: decrease of 25.3% to 27,832 units (H1 2025:\nL302@P9: 37,250 units). Sales performance recorded at\nL303@P9: 16.6%.\nL304@P9: Landed properties account for 55.6% (15,480\nL305@P9: units) of the total new launches, while stratified\nL306@P9: properties represent 44.4% (12,352 units).\nL307@P9: The trend of new residential launches from H1\nL308@P9: 2023 to H1 2026 is illustrated in Chart 1.\nL309@P9: In the first half of 2026, the highest number of\nL310@P9: new launches was recorded in Selangor, totaling\nL311@P9: 8,354 units, followed by Johor and Pulau Pinang\nL312@P9: with 6,697 units and 2,878 units, respectively.\nL313@P9: Property type of condominium/ apartment\nL314@P9: dominates the number of new launches for the\nL315@P9: first half of 2026, accounting for 41.4% of the\nL316@P9: total new launches. Meanwhile, two and three\nL317@P9: storey terrace house and single storey terraces\nL318@P9: house make up 31.7% and 15.2% respectively.\nL319@P9: Residential properties priced RM500,001 to\nL320@P9: RM1,000,000 dominate the newly launched\nL321@P9: market share at 57.1% (15,905 units), followed\nL322@P9: by 28.2% of properties priced RM300,000 and\nL323@P9: below (7,856 units), 12.7% for properties priced\nL324@P9: RM300,001 to RM500,000 (3,534 units), and\nL325@P9: the remaining portion consists of properties\nL326@P9-10: exceeding RM1,000,000 (537 units). 11 | Laporan Status Pasaran Harta\nL327@P10: Chart 1: Trend of Newly Launched Residential H1 2023 – H1 2026\nL328@P10-11: Chart 2: Volume of Newly Launched Residential by State H1 2026Laporan Status Pasaran Harta | 12\nL329@P11: Chart 4: Newly Launched Residential by Price Range H1 2026\nL330@P11-12: Chart 3: New Residential Units Launched by Property Type H1 2026 13 | Laporan Status Pasaran Harta\nL331@P12: 1.2 Kediaman Siap Belum Terjual\nL332@P12: Bagi separuh pertama tahun 2026 (H1 2026),\nL333@P12: sebanyak 33,094 unit kediaman siap belum\nL334@P12: terjual telah direkodkan dengan nilai keseluruhan\nL335@P12: berjumlah RM17.78 bilion. Jumlah ini menunjukkan\nL336@P12: peningkatan tahun ke tahun 23.0% dari segi\nL337@P12: bilangan dan 8.2% dari segi nilai berbanding\nL338@P12: tempoh yang sama pada tahun 2025 (H1 2025:\nL339@P12: 26,911 unit, RM16.44 bilion).\nL340@P12: Johor mencatatkan jumlah kediaman siap belum\nL341@P12: terjual tertinggi iaitu 4,222 unit (12.8%), diikuti\nL342@P12: Selangor 4,185 unit (12.6%) dan Perak 4,075 unit\nL343@P12: (12.3%).\nL344@P12: Berdasarkan jenis harta tanah, kondominium\nL345@P12: dan pangsapuri merupakan kategori tertinggi\nL346@P12: dalam senarai siap belum terjual, melibatkan\nL347@P12: 14,160 unit (42.8%). Rumah teres menyumbang\nL348@P12: 11,547 unit (34.9%), manakala rumah berkembar\nL349@P12: menyumbang sebanyak 3,124 unit (9.4%), diikuti\nL350@P12: rumah kluster sebanyak 1,411 unit (4.3%) dan\nL351@P12: rumah sesebuah 1,071 unit (3.2%). Selebihnya,\nL352@P12: iaitu 5.4% terdiri daripada lain-lain jenis kediaman.\nL353@P12: Unit kediaman siap belum terjual mengikut jenis\nL354@P12: ditunjukkan di Carta 8.\nL355@P12: Berdasarkan julat harga, harta tanah berharga\nL356@P12: RM300,000 dan ke bawah membentuk peratusan\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://napic.jpph.gov.my/storage/app/media//3-penerbitan/Shahrul/Bahagian%20Inventori%20Harta%20Tanah/Laporan%20Jadual%20Stok%20Harta%20Tanah/Q2%202026/Laporan%20Stok%20Harta%20Tanah%20H1%202026.pdf)\nciteturn268view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 43; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn267view0\",\"id\":19}); Total lines: 1924\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://napic.jpph.gov.my/storage/app/media//3-penerbitan/Shahrul/Bahagian%20Indeks%20Harta%20Tanah/Laporan%20Jadual%20SAPI/Q2%202026/SA-PI%20Report%20Q1%20-%20Q2%202026P.pdf)\nciteturn268view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 15; S